+# Complete positive financial report expectations
+
+Status: **post-adoption independent literal expectations; all actual consumers UNRUN**. This new packet contains two complete Programs, three complete Executions and six complete accepted CLI envelopes. It preserves the original seven financial-pair v2 payloads byte for byte. No earlier fixture, freeze, test, failure, observation or acceptance counter was changed.
+
+The review predicate is exact full Program equality and exact full accepted ordinary/metered report equality for collect47, its linked collect80 successor and allocate50 with bondAmount7. A future consumer must compare all fields and ordered arrays, plus the separately frozen stdout bytes, and retain any difference. This packet supplies expectations, not observed results or permission to execute a consumer.
+
+## Authority and independence
+
+`basis/DESIGN-ADOPTION.json` selects the unchanged financial clauses in `basis/financial-observation-clauses.md`, excerpted only from REVIEW-PACKET.md lines17–65. The proposal retains its historical unadopted labels; the later decision adopts it. Its implementation excerpts were not inspected. The source author/design reviewers disclosed implementation exposure. This derivation is post-adoption and public-source/DTO exposed, neither blinded nor preimplementation. The custodian read literal source, original independently authored financial fixtures, public grammar, serialized DTO definitions and the earlier independent representation/byte derivations. No parser, evaluator, compiler or exporter implementation, test implementation, proposed consumer, generated IR, actual Execution or actual stdout was used to select expectations. No Moriarty product was invoked. Plain Python copied bytes, assembled explicitly chosen literal JSON, serialized JSON and checked arithmetic/hashes.
+
+Development startup, AGENTS, product contract, roadmap/requirements and read-only status were restored. Historical SP01 blockers remain. Output is confined to this new outside-Git directory; no checkout/Git mutation, network, build, model, SDK, VM, proof, wallet, key or private-record operation occurred.
+
+The seven copied current `crates/fixtures/financial-pair` payloads exactly match W/docs/utxo/doctorwatson/oracles/financial-pair-v2. The original v2 inventory SHA is `7e5b09d844861f71ebaf04f56f011ec520d9defb2f0ae87b1ee6e626cea77f5e`. `prior-financial-and-work.json` and `prior-mori-tests.json` retain their original names/claims internally, including historically unresolved fields. New adoption resolves selected report fields prospectively; it does not rewrite that earlier record. No test code was read.
+
+The adoption's `proposalPacketSha256` identifies the whole design-review `MANIFEST.json` (SHA `f7dc6ba284578a42ac17be75ac2ceab60a0e40e425c808d0fceea593cf393735`), rather than the individual REVIEW-PACKET.md. That manifest binds REVIEW-PACKET.md SHA `6c859b7e773da1cb50e7205893e34cbd668f664a70cc50428f58364d2311d571` and the proposal patch SHA recorded in the adoption. A first pre-freeze binding assertion mistakenly compared these different hash subjects and stopped. Reading the manifest metadata resolved the subject distinction; no golden value changed, no frozen file was overwritten, and no product check failed. The manifest is copied as metadata only: its listed parser/runtime/test paths do not mean those bodies were read. The root's separate identity clarification records the same distinction; original adoption bytes remain untouched.
+
+## Explicit Program representation premises
+
+Public Program has exactly language, semantics, name, states, assets, expressions and actions. Profiles are moriarty/1 and moriarty-core/1. State/asset/action/input vectors preserve source declaration order; each action's statements preserve written order. State initializers are direct typed StateDecl literals, outside the arena. Every lexical expression occurrence allocates a fresh node, with children left to right before their enclosing operator, across all actions in source order. Parentheses allocate no node; repeated names/literals are not interned. These are explicit finite parser-comparison premises inherited from the adopted normal illustration and PR203 independent DERIVATION, not a claim that public Vec types alone establish a universal allocation algorithm. Actual parser correspondence is a future test predicate. All concrete selected IDs are resolved under these disclosed premises.
+
+Each Expr is exactly its public tagged variant; array index is its ExprId, with no added id member. Binary operators use public enum names. Full AssetId has network/issuer/reference/scale. Program includes uninvoked register actions and their literals/identity declarations. No scenario, selected action, financial frame, source hash, cost field or synthetic liability registry is added to Program. The file hashes identify expectation bytes; they are not an implementation canonical Program hash or compiler identity.
+
+Invoice has 32 expression nodes, numbered0..31. Register roots0/1 are literal127/9. Collect roots are **4,7,12,13,14,15,16,19,22,25,30,31**. Nodes2..4 are amount,0,Gt; 5..7 atDay,dueDay,Ge; 8..12 LiabilityPresent(invoice),LiabilityAmount(invoice),amount,Ge(9,10),And(8,11). Node13 captures opening; 14 amount; 15 literal3; 16 amount. Nodes17..19 paid,amount,Add; 20..22 dueDay,30,Add; 23..25 installments,1,Add. Nodes26..30 LiabilityAmount(invoice),opening,amount,Sub(27,28),Eq(26,29). Node31 reads paid for Emit. Full literal expected Program retains every node and edge.
+
